-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Arms): Improved Slam -- 0.75 / 1.5 sec
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Improved Slam (3, 6): Decreases the swing time of your Slam
--           ability by 0.75/1.5 sec. (2 ranks)"
--
-- Stock is 0.5 / 1.0 sec.  Slam's base cast is 1.5 sec, so rank 2 now makes it
-- instant.  That is the intent of the change, not an overshoot.
--
-- This is base points and nothing else.  The mechanism is already exactly what
-- is wanted: SPELL_AURA_ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER (107) with EffectMiscValue1 = 10
-- (SPELLMOD_CASTING_TIME), value in milliseconds.
--
-- Base points follow the N-1 convention, and the sign is carried through it:
-- -751 gives CalcValue -750, -1501 gives -1500.
--
-- The description is deliberately left as Blizzard wrote it.  "$/1000;S1"
-- divides the magnitude by 1000, so the existing text renders 0.75 and 1.5 with
-- no edit -- the number has one source, the DBC row.
--
-- EffectSpellClassMaskA1 and EffectSpellClassMaskB1 are both 0x200000 and are
-- left alone.  They are load-bearing for Slam's rank chain, and they are
-- exactly the fields a --base clone would silently mangle.
--
-- Spells:
--   12862 = Improved Slam Rank 1 (-750 ms)
--   12330 = Improved Slam Rank 2 (-1500 ms)   -- note: NOT in numeric rank order
-- ============================================================

DELETE FROM `alonecraft_spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (12862, 12330);
